# The system the root task starts at boot. One program per line:
#
#   name      process name (also how the console labels its output)
#   image     boot module holding its ELF executable
#   priority  1..250; no higher than the root task's
#   provides  service it serves on the endpoint in its slot 1, or -
#   uses      services it may call, comma-separated, or -; they land in
#             slots 2, 3, ... in this order, each with its own badge
#   devices   hardware it drives (com1), or -; it gets a notification in
#             slot 8 and each device's capabilities from slot 9 on
#   arg       number passed to main()
#
# name      image         priority  provides  uses      devices  arg
console     console.elf   200       console   -         com1     0
hello       hello.elf     100       -         console   -        0
